   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: The Brenwe Hydropower Plant (Output 1) and 40.5km transmission and distribution lines (Output 2) in Malekula were commissioned in October 2023. 45km of transmission and distribution lines in Espiritu Santo (Output) are expected to be commissioned in August 2024.Construction start of the LV line component in Malekula (Output 2) is expected in Q4 2024. A Project Management Consultant, who will support the LV reticulation design and procurement, is currently under recruitment. The Department of Energy is undertaking consultations with the utilities in Malekula and Espiritu Santo to facilitate an additional 1,050 household connections (Output 2).The Vanuatu Project Management Unit (VPMU) has received (i) gender training awareness, (ii) HIV/AIDS-STI training awareness, and (iii) SEAH training while further training on budgeting and business skills and power safety awareness will be provided for newly connected households (Output 3).</narrative>
    </title>
